---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Services · borck.consulting" pageClass="page">

  <div class="hero">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">Services</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title">Fixed-scope, fixed-price engagements for regulated practices.</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      The practice operates with one purchasable engagement at any given time, currently the
      AI Readiness Diagnostic. Other engagements are available to clients who have completed
      a Diagnostic and want to take the next step.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">Methodology</span>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-sub" style="max-width: none;">
      Every Diagnostic is structured around five strategic questions, drawn from the
      AI strategy literature (particularly Upadhyay's <em>Artificial Intelligence for
      Managers</em>, 2021, and Yao &amp; Koidan's <em>Applied Artificial Intelligence</em>,
      2024) and applied with the <em>Conversation not Delegation</em> framework as the
      operating principle. The methodology is a delivery practice, not a marketing claim:
      every Diagnostic deliverable answers each of the questions below in the firm's
      own terms.
    </p>

    <div class="tier-grid" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Question 1</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Can we do AI?</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          Maturity assessment of the firm's current capability across strategy,
          data, infrastructure, talent, governance, and culture. The starting point:
          what the firm is actually equipped to take on.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Question 2</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Should we do AI?</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          Opportunity analysis of where AI would create defensible value for
          <em>this</em> firm, and where it would create more risk than it removes.
          Not every viable use case is worth pursuing.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Question 3</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">How do we do AI?</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          Implementation orientation. What sequence, what gates, what
          change-management response. The practical move from <em>what</em>
          to <em>how</em>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Question 4</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Are we ready?</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          Infrastructure check. The data, the technology stack, the talent,
          and the gap between what the chosen path needs and what the firm
          currently has.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Question 5</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">What's the value?</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          Business case in the firm's own terms. Cost, return, risk reduction,
          scenario range. What the work is worth, in numbers leadership can defend.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--gray-2);">
      Long-form treatments of each question are published in
      <a href="/writing">writing</a>; practical techniques and frameworks
      that complement the methodology are in <a href="/resources">resources</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">Available Now</span>
    </div>

    <div class="offer-card primary" id="diagnostic">
      <div class="offer-eyebrow">Tier 0 · Bridge</div>
      <h2 class="offer-title">AI Readiness Diagnostic</h2>
      <p class="offer-price">
        AU$1,500 fixed
        <span class="qualifier">· 50% deposit, 50% on delivery</span>
      </p>
      <p class="offer-desc">
        A two-hour structured conversation with your leadership team, plus a 2&ndash;3 page
        written recommendation. The Diagnostic answers the question many partners are quietly
        asking themselves: <em>do we actually need to do anything yet?</em> The recommendation
        places your firm on the literacy &rarr; governance &rarr; sovereignty journey and
        identifies the single highest-leverage first move.
      </p>
      <div class="offer-includes">
        <ul>
          <li>2-hour structured conversation, in person (Perth) or remote (national)</li>
          <li>Written report with specific, firm-tailored recommendations</li>
          <li>One follow-up email exchange to clarify the report</li>
          <li>NDA available on request; all material handled per the practice's data policy</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a Diagnostic</a>
    </div>

    <div class="offer-card" style="margin-top: 2rem; background: var(--bg);">
      <div class="offer-eyebrow">Free · No email required</div>
      <h2 class="offer-title" style="font-size: 1.15rem;">Not sure if you need a Diagnostic?</h2>
      <p class="offer-desc" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Download the <strong>AI Readiness Reflection</strong> &mdash; a 3&ndash;4 page
        self-reflection prompt covering the kinds of questions a paid Diagnostic would
        ask. Use it alone or with your partners. If you can answer most of the questions
        confidently, you may not need a paid Diagnostic. If you cannot, that is also a
        useful conclusion.
      </p>
      <a href="/pre-diagnostic-reflection.pdf" class="btn-secondary btn">Download the Reflection (PDF)</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">Available After a Diagnostic</span>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-sub" style="margin-bottom: 2rem; max-width: none;">
      The engagements below are available to clients who have completed an AI Readiness
      Diagnostic and want to act on its recommendation. Each is fixed-scope, fixed-price,
      and shaped to the firm by the Diagnostic that precedes it.
    </p>

    <div class="offer-card">
      <div class="offer-eyebrow">Tier 1 · Foundation</div>
      <h2 class="offer-title">Half-day Conversation-not-Delegation Workshop</h2>
      <p class="offer-price">
        From AU$2,500 fixed
        <span class="qualifier">· scoped per firm</span>
      </p>
      <p class="offer-desc">
        Single-firm half-day workshop for the partner group and senior staff (10&ndash;50
        attendees). Establishes the firm's shared position on AI use through the
        Conversation-not-Delegation framework and its conversation loop (brainstorm, ideate,
        iterate, amplify), and equips the team with working prompts and protocols. Delivered in person in
        Perth or remotely nationally.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="offer-card">
      <div class="offer-eyebrow">Tier 2 · Governance</div>
      <h2 class="offer-title">AI Governance Starter</h2>
      <p class="offer-price">
        From AU$8,000 fixed
        <span class="qualifier">· 3-week engagement</span>
      </p>
      <p class="offer-desc">
        Three-week engagement producing an AI use policy specific to how the firm operates,
        a governance audit identifying current exposure, and a 90-day implementation roadmap.
        Includes a half-day Q&amp;A session with leadership before sign-off. The output is
        not a template; it is a policy the firm can defend to clients and regulators.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="offer-card">
      <div class="offer-eyebrow">Tier 3 · Sovereignty</div>
      <h2 class="offer-title">Local AI Readiness Assessment</h2>
      <p class="offer-price">
        From AU$6,000 fixed
        <span class="qualifier">· 1-week engagement</span>
      </p>
      <p class="offer-desc">
        One-week engagement covering data-sensitivity audit, current-state review of AI
        deployment, and a written report with indicative hardware and software plan for
        local-AI workloads. Implementation itself is explicitly out of scope; the output
        is the credible answer to <em>"what would we do with a matter we cannot route
        through any cloud service?"</em>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">Out of Scope</span>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-sub" style="max-width: none;">
      The practice does not undertake the following work, and this is unlikely to change:
    </p>
    <div class="offer-includes" style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--gray-1);">
      <ul>
        <li>Enterprise (more than 200 staff) and government tender work</li>
        <li>Hourly billing or staff augmentation</li>
        <li>Open-ended bespoke implementation or ongoing managed services</li>
        <li>Engagements scoped specifically as marketing or sales-effectiveness AI projects</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

</Base>
